# Export default: the red, the live pair and the scope, Runtime flow
#
# WHAT LANDS. An entry whose feature groups meet C.EXPORT_DEFAULT_FEATURE_GROUPS writes the per-record export
# without naming the plusarg. The scope is ("irq",), ruled by the Orchestrator; widening is adding a group name.
#
# WHY. A checker fire is diagnosed from the record stream and nothing else in the run directory retains one. Of
# the 403-run wave at 4017573, 96 runs failed: 75 were fcov-expectation failures whose result.yaml names the
# missing bins and needed no re-run, and 21 were checker or assertion fires that did. All 21 are gen_test_irq_basic
# and its red fixture. That measurement is the scope's justification and it is why the default is not wider.
#
# ONE READING THE ORCHESTRATOR SHOULD SEE RATHER THAN FIND. The ruling's words were "entries carrying a fire
# check (the irq family)". In this tree a fire check is the fire_check() hook, which every gen_test_ entry has,
# so that reading covers 54 of round 2's 56 planned runs and CONTAINS every measured entry, which is the scope
# the same ruling excluded. The parenthetical is the reading that satisfies both halves, and it is the one built.

================================================================
# SECTION 1: THE RED, live, on one entry and one seed
# stamp 2026-09-05T12:26:24Z  host soc-l-11  driver trees are archives of edbe8214c15893ec2c083d5a9938aafab5893103
#
# Same entry, same seed, same already-built simv, same mirror. The two driver trees differ in exactly four
# files: gen_flow_const.py, gen_flow_util.py, gen_run.py, gen_regress.py. Nothing else varies.
#   build   /proj_soc/user_dev/fzhang/ibex_dv_out/regress_chkfix/build/gen_tb  (compiled at 9c7f8f6)
#   mirror  /proj_soc/user_dev/fzhang/ibex_dv_mirror_head/9c7f8f63957d, checked by the run against the build's record
#   entry   gen_test_irq_basic   seed 1005939007   testlist taken from the mirror for BOTH runs

PRE  (committed flow code)
    verdict        PASS
    reason         no collected failure mechanism; end marker and config banner present
    export_file    None
    export_origin  None
    header sources None
    gen_export.txt ABSENT from the run directory

POST (the change)
    verdict        PASS
    reason         no collected failure mechanism; end marker and config banner present
    export_file    /proj_soc/user_dev/fzhang/ibex_dv_out/expdef_red/post/gen_test_irq_basic_1005939007/gen_export.txt
    export_origin  default
    header sources ['ibus', 'dbus', 'pin', 'alert', 'misc', 'scrkey', 'regime']
    gen_export.txt present, 152068 bytes

RED: the pre-change run records export_file null and its run directory holds no gen_export.txt, so a checker
fire in that run would leave nothing per-record behind. GREEN: the post-change run writes the stream and says
the name came from the default rather than from a choice.

THE VERDICT IS UNCHANGED, AND THAT WAS THE RISK WORTH CHECKING. export_check fails a PASS run that names an
export file and writes none or writes one without a header, so a default turned on carelessly could turn passing
runs into failures. It does not: the header carries all seven sources the build declares and the check passes.

